<!--
  SNO+-like detector for OpticalSims (RiceOpticks / Opticks). Generated 2026-10-13 by make_snoplus_gdml.py.
  AV centre = origin. Cavity water 22 m x 34 m; acrylic sphere R_in 6005 mm, wall 55 mm,
  neck R_in 730 mm x 6800 mm; LAB + 2 g/L PPO (11900 photons/MeV) filled to z = 7000 mm,
  N2 above; opaque PSUP shell R 8360-8890 mm; 9362 inward PMTs (dome R 130 mm at r = 8350 mm,
  uniform Fibonacci layout - not the real SNO+ positions). Sensor: volPMT, SensDet = PhotonDetector, copynumber = sensor id.
  Scintillation time constants 4.88 / 15.40 / 165.1 ns, yields 0.664 / 0.218 / 0.118.
  PMT EFFICIENCY = bialkali QE x 0.952 (concentrator collection, 54% effective coverage).
  References: arXiv:2104.11687 (SNO+), nucl-ex/9910016 (SNO NIM), arXiv:2011.12924 (SNO+ LS), arXiv:1105.2101 (LAB n).
  Approximate inputs: LS absorption and emission shape, acrylic absorption, PMT layout, QE (Super-K bialkali curve).
-->
